<title>JAPAN: IADB launches 3.0% yen/A$ reverse dual samurais.</title>
<headline>IADB launches 3.0% yen/A$ reverse dual samurais.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following yen/Australian dollar reverse dual-currency samurai issue was announced by lead manager Nomura Securities on Thursday:</p>
<p> BORROWER	  Inter-American Development Bank</p>
<p> AMT		 15 bln yen</p>
<p> COUPON	    3.0 pct</p>
<p> ISS PRICE	 par</p>
<p> MATURITY	  16 March 2007</p>
<p> PAY DATE	  18 March 1997</p>
<p> SUB PERIOD	March 13 to March 14</p>
<p> PAY FREQ	  Annual</p>
<p> LAST RATING     S&amp;P AAA, Moody's Aaa</p>
<p> LEAD MANAGER    Nomura Securities</p>
<p> LEAD TRUSTEE    N/A</p>
<p>NOTE: The coupon will be paid in Australian dollars, while redemption will be in yen. The exchange rate was fixed at A$5,310.67/500,000 yen.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-3432-8785</p>
</text>
